<article class="env-example" id="02WB">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02WB">Example <span data-tag="02WB">7.1.3.10</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category and let $f: X \rightarrow Y$ be a morphism of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. The following conditions are equivalent: </p>
<p><ul>
<li><p>
The morphism $f$ is an isomorphism. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
When regarded as a morphism $(\Delta ^0)^{\triangleleft } \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, $f$ is a limit diagram. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
When regarded as a morphism $(\Delta ^0)^{\triangleright } \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, $f$ is a colimit diagram. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
<p> This is a restatement of Proposition <a data-tag="02J2" href="/tag/02J2">4.7.3.20</a> (and also of Example <a data-tag="02JR" href="/tag/02JR">7.1.1.6</a>, by virtue of Remark <a data-tag="02WA" href="/tag/02WA">7.1.3.6</a>). </p>
</article>
